# One person, one entry.
#
# Git identity is whatever `user.name` and `user.email` were set to on the
# machine that made the commit, so the same person becomes two contributors the
# first time they use a different laptop. This file is where that is corrected,
# and it corrects it everywhere at once: `git shortlog`, `git log %aN`, the
# generated CONTRIBUTORS.md, and GitHub's own blame all read it.
#
# Format: the canonical identity first, then the one to fold into it.
#
#     Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Other Name <other@email>
#
# Adding an entry rewrites no history and changes no commit; it only changes how
# the same commits are attributed when they are read.

irene-the-best <xxiellan@gmail.com> Irene <xxiellan@gmail.com>
